Subject: [PATCH] Lichii #880 via Fritchii: a texture cache image that does not fit is left out instead of unbacked (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_UNBACKED, off by default)

Port of zortos293/Lichii#880 (a07eed1ad9, by zortos293, merged 2026-11-08) as cherry-picked into
Frizti/Fritchii 73880e166a (v5 "RAM cuts" merge b8338f4241).

With EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_UNBACKED=1, MemoryAllocator::CreateImage no longer gives an image that the
texture cache can do without an unbacked sparse stand-in when no memory is left (reads zero,
writes dropped; drawing into one is what AMD drivers, RADV included, do not survive). It throws
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY instead, and our existing refusal path takes it:
TextureCacheRuntime::SurvivesImageRefusal returns false and JoinImages leaves the image out ("No
memory for the image ... left out", 1 s pause for that size or larger; EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT
retries as before), so the image is made again at a later use once the collector freed memory.
The console's own steps before the fallback (prepare-vulkan-port.py: ReleaseRefused retry,
NoFallbackLeft / EDEN_NX2_UNBACKED_LIMIT accounting) run unchanged first; only the unbacked
fallback is replaced. Images over 2^28 texels (never backed) and every other caller keep it.

Deviations: upstream adds may_fail to AllocateImage/TryCreateImage; this tree throws through
SlotVector::insert instead (the console's copy throws, headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake, as
0169-oom-fix-02 relies on), so the "may fail" state is a thread_local set by an RAII scope only
around JoinImages' make_image inside SurvivesImageRefusal, and never when a refusal ends the
session (ImageRefusalEnds). The allocator anchor line the generator replaces is untouched; the check
sits inside that block, after the console's retry. Not ported: #880's UNIMPLEMENTED() skip for
remapped GPU-modified overlaps (a log line), the MaxBackedImageTexels rename in Image::Image.

Checks (fritchii-unbacked_checks.sh, log fritchii-unbacked.checks.log): git apply --check on
$R/Eglantine; 6 anchor skips before and after (same); only the generated vulkan_memory_allocator.cpp
differs and holds the check inside the console's "&& !no_fallback" block; -fsyntax-only of the
generated allocator, vk_texture_cache_cost, vk_texture_cache_base (Vulkan instantiation),
vulkan_rasterizer, vulkan_renderer, blit_image: rc=0; injected static_asserts and injected calls in
SurvivesImageRefusal (instantiated) and the generated allocator all reported; host unit test
fritchii-unbacked_test.cpp (#880's cases, the scope through an exception, the switch) passes, fails
on a wrong expectation and does not build against T81b.

Expected effect: in the recent PS5 runs 31 of 323 logged "does not fit; using an unbacked sparse
image" (1280x720 format 97/126, 2560x1440 122/126) and 10 of those 31 crashed: a missing target for
a frame instead. Memory is not created. Risk: black or partial frames under memory pressure.

